<p>Last year under the Whiny Little Bitch name, and the year the weekly-high
hundred showed up to give the also-rans something to lie about. Michael put up the
most points in the league and actually won the whole thing, which almost never
happens here and confused everyone.</p>

<h3><span class="n">§</span> The Fraud</h3>
<p>Cory went 9-6 and cashed on the worst-scoring team in the league. His all-play
was <span class="stat">.422</span>, a 57-78 record against the field, and he still
walked out with <span class="stat">$400</span>. The team was named "Herbert the
Pervert," which is the most honest thing about that season.</p>

<h3><span class="n">§</span> The Robbed</h3>
<p>Justin went 71-64 against the field, better than half the guys who made money,
and finished 6-9 with <span class="stat">$0</span>. Meanwhile David dropped
<span class="stat">140.76</span> in a loss to Michael, benched Justin Fields for
40.98 in a week his starters mustered 69.12, and missed a weekly-high by
<span class="stat">0.52</span>. He scored 171.50 in Week 4, blew Sam out by 98.40,
and still finished second.</p>

<h3><span class="n">§</span> The Weird</h3>
<p>Jeremy had the best single game of the year — C.J. Stroud for
<span class="stat">51.80</span> — and went 5-10 with a seven-game losing streak.
Bates opened the season with 52.20, the lowest score anyone posted all year. Dylan
made the championship game and lost it, the closest he's ever gotten and probably
ever will.</p>

<div class="respect"><p class="crown">The Champion</p><p>Michael went 95-40
against the field, the best in the league, backed it with the highest point total
at <span class="stat">1852.22</span>, and won it clean for
<span class="stat">$1050</span>. First of his.</p></div>

<p>Everybody paid, Michael took the pile, and Cory got four hundred dollars for
finishing dead last in scoring. The hundred for weekly-high was new and
immediately mocked.</p>
